{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Link"},{"type":"text","value":" component is a component that can be used to create a link that can be used to navigate to a new location. This includes changes to the pathname, search params, hash, and location state."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"link-props","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Link props"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Link"},{"type":"text","value":" component accepts the following props:"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"props","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"...props"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"LinkProps & React.RefAttributes<HTMLAnchorElement>"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./LinkPropsType.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"LinkProps"}]}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"link-returns","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Link returns"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"An anchor element that can be used to navigate to a new location."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"examples","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Examples"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { Link } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nfunction Component() {\n  return (\n    <Link\n      to=\"/somewhere/$somewhereId\"\n      params={{ somewhereId: 'baz' }}\n      search={(prev) => ({ ...prev, foo: 'bar' })}\n    >\n      Click me\n    </Link>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"By default, param values with characters such as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@"},{"type":"text","value":" will be encoded in the URL:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// url path will be `/%40foo`\n<Link to=\"/$username\" params={{ username: '@foo' }} />","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"To opt out, set "},{"type":"link","href":"../router/RouterOptionsType#pathparamsallowedcharacters-property","children":[{"type":"text","value":"pathParamsAllowedCharacters"}]},{"type":"text","value":" when creating the router. This setting cannot be changed on an existing router instance."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { createRouter } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nconst router = createRouter({\n  routeTree,\n  pathParamsAllowedCharacters: ['@'],\n})","lang":"tsx"}],"headings":[{"id":"link-props","text":"Link props","level":2},{"id":"props","text":"...props","level":3},{"id":"link-returns","text":"Link returns","level":2},{"id":"examples","text":"Examples","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nThe `Link` component is a component that can be used to create a link that can be used to navigate to a new location. This includes changes to the pathname, search params, hash, and location state.\n\n## Link props\n\nThe `Link` component accepts the following props:\n\n### `...props`\n\n- Type: `LinkProps & React.RefAttributes<HTMLAnchorElement>`\n- [`LinkProps`](./LinkPropsType.md)\n\n## Link returns\n\nAn anchor element that can be used to navigate to a new location.\n\n## Examples\n\n```tsx\nimport { Link } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nfunction Component() {\n  return (\n    <Link\n      to=\"/somewhere/$somewhereId\"\n      params={{ somewhereId: 'baz' }}\n      search={(prev) => ({ ...prev, foo: 'bar' })}\n    >\n      Click me\n    </Link>\n  )\n}\n```\n\nBy default, param values with characters such as `@` will be encoded in the URL:\n\n```tsx\n// url path will be `/%40foo`\n<Link to=\"/$username\" params={{ username: '@foo' }} />\n```\n\nTo opt out, set [pathParamsAllowedCharacters](../router/RouterOptionsType#pathparamsallowedcharacters-property) when creating the router. This setting cannot be changed on an existing router instance.\n\n```tsx\nimport { createRouter } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nconst router = createRouter({\n  routeTree,\n  pathParamsAllowedCharacters: ['@'],\n})\n```\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: linkComponent\ntitle: Link component\n---\n\nThe `Link` component is a component that can be used to create a link that can be used to navigate to a new location. This includes changes to the pathname, search params, hash, and location state.\n\n## Link props\n\nThe `Link` component accepts the following props:\n\n### `...props`\n\n- Type: `LinkProps & React.RefAttributes<HTMLAnchorElement>`\n- [`LinkProps`](./LinkPropsType.md)\n\n## Link returns\n\nAn anchor element that can be used to navigate to a new location.\n\n## Examples\n\n```tsx\nimport { Link } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nfunction Component() {\n  return (\n    <Link\n      to=\"/somewhere/$somewhereId\"\n      params={{ somewhereId: 'baz' }}\n      search={(prev) => ({ ...prev, foo: 'bar' })}\n    >\n      Click me\n    </Link>\n  )\n}\n```\n\nBy default, param values with characters such as `@` will be encoded in the URL:\n\n```tsx\n// url path will be `/%40foo`\n<Link to=\"/$username\" params={{ username: '@foo' }} />\n```\n\nTo opt out, set [pathParamsAllowedCharacters](../router/RouterOptionsType#pathparamsallowedcharacters-property) when creating the router. This setting cannot be changed on an existing router instance.\n\n```tsx\nimport { createRouter } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nconst router = createRouter({\n  routeTree,\n  pathParamsAllowedCharacters: ['@'],\n})\n```\n"}
